# AnyPS2 agent entry point

Read AGENTS.md for authoritative engineering, testing, and provenance instructions.
Read DISCLAIMER.md before handling game inputs.

AnyPS2 targets a fast, modern native PC program. Convert EE, IOP and VU code into
typed IR and compile ahead of time through LLVM. Keep the tool and shared native
services in clean C++20. LLVM is the only output backend. Do not generate C++ game code or maintain
a selectable C++ conversion fallback.

Do not ship an interpreter, JIT, emulator wrapper or emulator fallback. Existing
IOP interpretation is diagnostic scaffolding to replace. Modernize supported
console operations into native PC systems, including Vulkan rendering, while
preserving observable game behaviour. Keep generated commercial content ignored.

Retain IR and reproducible build configuration locally. Verify the compiled
executable and its dependencies; source emission or compilation alone is not game
compatibility or measured performance. Run only relevant milestone tests after cohesive operation-family batches, not after each opcode.
